/avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/367227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet","html_url":"https://github.com/Groovounet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":2,"closed_issues":212,"state":"open","created_at":"2012-09-12T10:39:38Z","updated_at":"2023-12-21T16:45:01Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":5,"created_at":"2018-01-16T19:53:38Z","updated_at":"2018-07-26T20:19:25Z","closed_at":"2018-07-24T22:24:30Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"It appears the == operator on vectors and matrices have changed behavior since the 0.9.8.5 release. If you run the following code snippet with 0.9.8.5 and then with the current master branch they do not produce the same results. Objects that used to be considered equal are no longer equal.\r\n\r\n----<snip>----\r\n#include <iostream>\r\n#include <glm/glm.hpp>\r\n\r\nint main(int argc, const char* arg[]) {\r\n\r\n  glm::vec2 a(0.0f, 1.0f);\r\n  glm::vec2 b(-0.0f, 1.0f);\r\n\r\n  std::cout << \"a == b : \" << (a == b) << std::endl;\r\n\r\n  std::cout << \"a.x == b.x && a.y == b.y : \"\r\n            << (a.x == b.x && a.y == b.y) << std::endl;\r\n  return 0;\r\n}\r\n----<snip>----\r\n\r\nIt appears the new behavior was introduced  by https://github.com/g-truc/glm/commit/384dab02e45a8ad3c1a3fa0906e0d5682c5b27b9 to silence compiler warnings, but this breaks compatibility and violates my expectation that an == operator is equivalent to per-element application of ==. \r\n\r\nI understand some folks may want this stricter form of equality, but could this at least be placed behind a feature define to avoid breaking existing code?\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Groovounet","id":367227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NzIyNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/367227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet","html_url":"https://github.com/Groovounet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/723/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/723/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}